separate the rendering from logic (rn lagging logic laggs the ui too) :
	Don't block the UI at all.
	The lock-holding-worker-thread design means any nonzero sweep time is a freeze.
	Kicking the logic to a separate thread (or dropping/reacquiring the sim lock between chunks) would keep rendering responsive during difficult stuff
	regardless of how fast the logic itself runs.


